  "notes": "USAGE:\nCommonly used in technical contexts (sensors, detectors, alarms) and also for the innate ability of people or animals to sense things that aren't immediately obvious.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {感知|かんち}する (to detect; to sense)\n- {感知器|かんちき} (detector; sensor)\n- {煙|けむり}{感知器|かんちき} (smoke detector)\n- {危険|きけん}を{感知|かんち}する (to sense danger)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {検知|けんち}: detection — more technical, used for instruments and scientific measurement\n- {察知|さっち}: perception; sensing — emphasizes intuiting something through observation or experience",
